{"availability":"available","full":"Chris0Jeky/MDviewer","name":"MDviewer","description":"Browser-based Markdown-to-PDF editor with live pagination and page-break-safe export for technical and research documents.","category":"Productivity","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-25T01:04:07Z","updated":"2026-10-07T02:26:45Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mdviewer-c9r.pages.dev/","topics":["browser-based","document-editor","markdown","markdown-to-pdf","pagedjs","pdf","privacy-first","technical-writing","typescript","vite"],"demo":"https://mdviewer-c9r.pages.dev/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:25.960Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:25.960Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:25.960Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T14:48:25.960Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Write Markdown, or drag a file in — get a beautiful PDF out, with no code block, figure, table, or callout ever sliced across a page boundary.","MDviewer is a browser-based Markdown → PDF tool built for research papers and code-heavy technical docs. Write in the built-in source pane and watch the paginated preview rebuild as you type, or drop a file in and edit it in place. It runs 100% in your browser: your documents are never uploaded, never stored on a server, and never sent anywhere. Same-origin application assets may load lazily as features run. The app itself persists only a small settings object in localStorage. The public site also sends pseudonymous, content-free usage data to the owner's own Pulseboard collector (never…","Typical online Markdown-to-PDF converters slice a code listing in half at the page break, orphan a table header, or cut a diagram down the middle. For a paper or a technical doc, that is unacceptable. MDviewer's #1 value proposition is the no-slice guarantee: atomic blocks stay whole, and when a block is genuinely taller than a page, it splits cleanly (repeated table headers, continuous frames, shrink-to-fit) instead of being chopped."],"features":["Syntax-highlighted code via Shiki (TextMate-grade, dual light/dark themes; print forces the light side for clean PDFs).","Math via KaTeX (inline and display; bad TeX renders red inline instead of breaking the document).","Diagrams via Mermaid (fixed-size SVG so pagination measures them correctly).","Callouts — note / tip / warning / danger admonition blocks.","Footnotes that float to the bottom of the page they are referenced on."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chris0Jeky/MDviewer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8938eb20033315369e29af2885a951522faae80025a726d1171c5f7ca79236cf","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:26.149Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:26.149Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Write Markdown, or drag a file in — get a beautiful PDF out, with no code block, figure, table, or callout ever sliced across a page boundary.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chris0Jeky/MDviewer/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"MDviewer is a browser-based Markdown → PDF tool built for research papers and code-heavy technical docs. Write in the built-in source pane and watch the paginated preview rebuild as you type, or drop a file in and edit it in place. It runs 100% in your browser: your documents are never uploaded, never stored on a server, and never sent anywhere. Same-origin application assets…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chris0Jeky/MDviewer/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"The live site ( only; local runs, previews and self-hosted copies send nothing) loads the Pulseboard SDK 3.3 from its own origin (/pulseboard.js) and sends data only to the owner's first-party collector.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chris0Jeky/MDviewer/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"8938eb20033315369e29af2885a951522faae80025a726d1171c5f7ca79236cf","sourceUrl":"https://github.co